# Line-ending form is pinned to LF for the kit's own hook/tool scripts
# and git-hook shell scripts, plus the two boot files this port's own
# tools/session_context.py measures BY ON-DISK BYTE SIZE (stat().st_size):
# BOOT BUDGET (boot_budget_lines()), the personal CLAUDE.md WARN
# threshold (CLAUDE_WARN), and the Layer A "on disk" byte figure
# (layer_a_lines()) all read the file's size straight off the
# filesystem -- a checkout that rewrites LF -> CRLF (or the reverse,
# core.autocrlf-dependent) silently changes that size and can move a
# WARN/OVER verdict without any real content change. Same class the
# staff deployment's own .gitattributes exists for (byte-budget
# measured by on-disk form -- docs/SIBLING_MAP.md, axis 14 there).
#
# Scripts: a CRLF shebang line under .githooks/ silently breaks hook
# execution on a Linux clone; a mixed CRLF/LF split was found on disk
# empirically across toolkit/tools/*.py and toolkit/.githooks/* during
# this port (2026-08-25) -- this pin normalizes checkouts going
# forward, it does not itself rewrite any file's current content.
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
BOOT.md text eol=lf
tools/*.py text eol=lf
plans/PILES.md text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
# Generated file compared byte-for-byte by `tools/factory_rules_index.py --check`
# (pre-commit): a CRLF checkout under core.autocrlf=true would read as stale forever.
docs/FACTORY_RULES_INDEX.md text eol=lf
# The same for `tools/architecture_index.py --check` (F6-29).
docs/ARCHITECTURE_INDEX.md text eol=lf
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
# The routing journal is append-only and two clones append at its tail: `merge=union` merges
# the two tails without a conflict (both sets of lines are kept). The union may interleave two
# sessions' lines, so tools/journal_validator.py's ts monotonicity can report such a merged
# tail; the commit that FOLLOWS the merge validates as before (tools/test_forge_metrics.py K7).
logs/routing-log.jsonl merge=union
# t-581: one journal file per writer, logs/journal/<slug>.jsonl. `union` covers the one case it can still
# meet -- one slug on two machines (the merge validator then WARNs "written by two clones"); `eol=lf`
# keeps a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true) from turning every line into an edit.
logs/journal/*.jsonl merge=union text eol=lf
# GM1-8: shell scripts and workflow files run on Linux; a CRLF shebang or YAML line breaks them there.
*.sh text eol=lf
docs/migration/**/*.yml text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml text eol=lf
